  "id": "mcp-host/a-header-the-transport-writes-or-cannot-send-is-refused-at-construction",
  "title": "A provider given a header its transport writes itself (framing, the content accepted and sent, mcp-*), an invalid header, a value past 8192 bytes or more than 32 headers is refused at construction; 32 headers of 8192 bytes are not",
  "rules": [
    "§21.2"
  ],
  "requirements": [
    "RK-21.2-011"
  ],
  "notes": "Python: tools/mcp.py _check_headers (_TRANSPORT_HEADERS, _MAX_HEADERS, _MAX_HEADER_VALUE_BYTES); roomkit-rs: roomkit-mcp provider/construction.rs. The 32 headers and 8192 bytes are the reference implementation's bounds, which the unit names. Each refusal is the call's invalid_argument, before any operation. The last two calls are built and only read connected, which opens nothing.",
